ous by nature very respectful  of cultures and he wanted to share with  the public his discoveries  the idea was do not be scared of  travelling and do not be scared of going  to other countries and do not stay at  the resort do not stay at the hotel and  eat the normal menu just go out go in  the streets engage with people try the  food and learn the culture from from  that experience and I think it is really  well in breaking walls right in between  US and other countries that we sometimes  are a bit scared or nervous to to visit  and that was really a great part of his  legacy yeah and he really didn't hold  much back right I mean he ever  criticized you are cooking no we used to  play pranks on each other and then we  used to have a lot of fun but never  criticize my food before we go one last  thing what's the one ingredient we  should all have in our kitchen olive oil  olive oil it's very healthy  it's very tasty you can apply it on so  many great dishes on salad on fish on  and it makes every vegetable taste  better and I know you're working on a  vegetable book as well yes  underrated food yes great to have you  congratulations congratulations on  everything for one
 

